==Strategy==
This stage is quite difficult to rush without very high level units (lv 55+ Can Can strong enough to kill Gabriels in 1 hit) or brute force without Anti-Aku/Shield Piercing cats.

If you are able to kill Vermilingua Rangmaster faster than the 2nd one spawns, then you are good to just brute force the rest of the stage. Anti-Aku meatshields such as [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Belly Dancer]] can hold Vermilingua Rangmaster at a distance for the DPS ubers to take him down quickly. Shield Piercing, Anti-Traited, or Anti-Aku Ubers can make up for not having a specialized meatshield.

[[Ancient Egg: N205 (Special Cat)|Bride Cat]] works wonders as a meatshield, especially if missing [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]], since she has Behemoth Slayer and Strong against both Zombies and Aku. While she is vulnerable to the Angel enemies here, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] already exists to counter Angels. Do note that she needs help from Research [[Cat Combo]]s because of her long 6.5 second recharge.

[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] is a great option if you don't have [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] by this point, as he outranges Rangmaster by a decent margin and has a lot of chances to land a Shield Pierce with his quick attack rate.

